        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.introduction", "§NIntroduction");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.introductioninfotext",
                "There's a lot going on in the Forge of the Gods, which can be quite confusing at first. This menu aims to explain everything that is happening and all the capabilities/mechanics of the forge.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.tableofcontents", "§NTable of Contents");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.fuel", "Fuel");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.modules", "Modules");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.upgrades", "Upgrades");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.milestones", "Milestones");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.inversion", "Inversion");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.fuelinfotext.1",
                "Once the structure of the Forge is built and the multiblock is formed, just simply turning it on is not sufficient to make it functional. The Forge must be supplied with a certain amount of §bStar Fuel §6(the item) to actually boot up.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.fuelinfotext.2",
                "The amount of Star Fuel needed depends on the current fuel consumption factor, which can be set in the fuel configuration menu. By default the maximum is 5, but it can be increased later on with upgrades. Star Fuel scaling is as follows:");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.fuelinfotext.3", "factor*25*1.2^factor");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.fuelinfotext.4",
                "Star Fuel can be supplied via an input bus, it gets consumed periodically and stored internally. Once there is enough Star Fuel stored in the multi, it turns on for real (allowing modules to connect) and converts the consumed Star Fuel into stored §bStellar Fuel§6.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.fuelinfotext.5",
                "From this point onwards, the Forge must be fueled via one of the liquid fuels (type can be selected in the fuel config menu). If there isn't enough of the selected fuel present in the input hatch, the stored fuel amount will decrease and if it reaches 0, the Forge enters the previous 'off' state where modules disconnect and it has to be supplied with Star Fuel again.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.fuelinfotext.6",
                "The amount of internally stored Stellar Fuel (liquid) can be increased by turning on §bBattery Charging§6, this will cause the fuel usage to double, but half of it will be stored in the internal battery.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.1",
                "There are 4 types of modules that can be used in the Forge, the Helioflare Power Forge, Helioflux Melting Core, Heliothermal Plasma Fabricator and Heliofusion Exoticizer. These modules are separate multiblocks that have to be built into the Forge's structure at their designated spots.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.2",
                "Once built, these modules have to connect to the Forge, which happens automatically if all requirements for the respective module are met. Alternatively, there is a button to refresh their status without waiting for the timer. Each of these modules has its specialized functionality & requirements and is affected differently by certain upgrades.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.forge.1", "Helioflare Power Forge");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.forge.2",
                "The first unlocked module, simply put is a blast furnace even more powerful than the Exothermic Hearth. Additionally, this module has a §bFurnace Mode§6, turning it into a hyper powerful Multi Smelter. This module is unlocked by default and has §b1024§6 base parallel.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.core.1", "Helioflux Melting Core");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.core.2",
                "The second unlocked module, which also processes blast furnace recipes but with a twist; the outputs are ejected in §bMolten form§6 instead of ingots. If an output does not have a molten form, it will output its regular form. This module has to be unlocked by an upgrade to function and has §b512§6 base parallel.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.fab.1", "Heliothermal Plasma Fabricator");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.fab.2",
                "The third unlocked module, which possesses a unique recipemap featuring direct material to plasma conversion recipes. These recipes are grouped by two properties, §bFusion Tier§6 and §bSteps Required§6, limiting which recipes can be processed before their respective upgrades are unlocked. Unlike regular fusion, these recipes produce the plasma of the input material. This module has §b512§6 base parallel.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.exotic.1", "Heliofusion Exoticizer");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.exotic.2",
                "The fourth and final unlocked module, capable of producing §bQuark Gluon Plasma§6 and later on §bMagmatter§6. This module has unique automation challenges for both materials, so it is recommended to have two of these, as they have to be locked to either one of the materials.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.exotic.3",
                "The common rule for both modes' automation challenges is as follows: the module outputs materials at the start of a recipe cycle and waits for the correct inputs to arrive before starting the actual processing of the output material.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.exotic.4",
                "If producing §bQuark Gluon Plasma§6, the module outputs up to 7 different fluids/dusts with amounts between 1-64 and 1-7 respectively, and their corresponding plasmas and amounts have to be returned in order for the recipe to process. For each L of fluid, a bucket of plasma and for each dust 9 ingots worth of plasma must be returned for the recipe to work.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.exotic.5",
                "If §bMagmatter Mode§6 is active, the automation challenge changes. Now the module outputs 1-50L of §bTachyon Rich Temporal Fluid§6, 51-100L of §bSpatially Enlarged Fluid§6 and one dust of a high tier material. The challenge is to return both the Tachyon Rich and Spatially Enlarged Fluids, plus as much plasma of the dust's material (in ingots) as the difference between the amounts of Spatially Enlarged and Tachyon Rich Fluid. Once all of these have been returned in the correct amounts, the recipe will start to process and output Magmatter.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.moduleinfotext.exotic.6", "This module has §b64§6 base parallel.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.upgradeinfotext.1",
                "Upgrades are the heart and soul of the Forge, they unlock most of its functionality and processing power. The §bUpgrade Tree§6 can be accessed via its button on the main GUI, and each upgrade node can be clicked for more information on its effects and unlock requirements.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.upgradeinfotext.2",
                "In general, each upgrade can only be unlocked if the prior one is unlocked and there are enough available §bGraviton Shards§6. One exception to this is the first upgrade, which has no prior upgrade. Some upgrades also have extra material costs, which are denoted next to the unlock button if applicable.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.upgradeinfotext.3",
                "If an upgrade has more than one connected prior upgrade, then there are two options. The upgrade requires either:");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.upgradeinfotext.4",
                "- All prior upgrades (§4Red§a connections)\n- At least one prior upgrade (§9Blue§a connections)");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.upgradeinfotext.5",
                "Upgrades can be refunded by pressing the §bRespec§6 button, but this only works if ALL connected later upgrades are not active/unlocked.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.upgradeinfotext.6",
                "The block of upgrades following the unlock of the Heliofusion Exoticizer module are special, as they are what is considered §bThe Split§6. As the name suggests, only one path out of the three may be chosen at first, and the others will be locked. Each path has specialized buffs that are primarily targeted towards a specific module, and thus affect other module types with reduced effect (unless stated otherwise). The amount of unlockable paths depends on the §bAmount of Rings§6 the Forge has, which in turn is limited by later upgrades.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.milestoneinfotext.1",
                "Milestones are essential for upgrading the Forge, as they are the source of §bGraviton Shards§6, the main currency needed for unlocking upgrades. In essence, milestones are just what their name suggests, thresholds that when reached, grant Graviton Shards.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.milestoneinfotext.2",
                "There are four types of milestones, Charge, Conversion, Catalyst and Composition, each referring to a stat of the Forge. Each milestone has §bseven§6 tiers, each being harder to reach than the last, but also granting more Graviton Shards. The first tier grants 1 Shard, the second 2, the third 3 and so on.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.milestoneinfotext.3",
                "The §bCharge§6 milestone scales off total power consumption of all modules combined, the first tier being unlocked at §b1e15§6 EU consumed, and each subsequent milestone scaling by §b9x§6.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.milestoneinfotext.4",
                "The §bConversion§6 milestone scales off total recipes processed across all modules (excluding the Helioflare Power Forge's furnace mode) and its first tier is unlocked at §b10M§6 processed recipes. Following tiers scale by §b4x§6.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.milestoneinfotext.5",
                "The §bCatalyst§6 milestone is based on the Forge's fuel consumption, counted in Stellar Fuel units (the number entered in the fuel config menu). Reaching the first tier requires §b10,000§6 fuel units to be consumed, and each tier above scales by §b3x§6.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.milestoneinfotext.6",
                "Last but not least, the §bComposition§6 milestone works a bit differently, as it scales off the Forge's structure. Milestone levels are granted for each unique type of module present in the structure (Heliofusion Exoticizer modules on Quark Gluon and Magmatter Modes count as unique), and for each additional ring built.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.milestoneinfotext.7",
                "Your research suggests that something strange might happen if all milestones reach their final tier... Make sure to check back!");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.inversioninfotext.1",
                "Once all milestones of the Forge reach §bTier 7§6, inversion activates. This uncaps the maximum tier of all milestones and allows it to scale §binfinitely§6.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.inversioninfotext.2",
                "The scaling of each milestone changes from exponential to linear, but the granted Graviton Shard amount keeps increasing. The amount of progress needed for each subsequent milestone is as much as needed for the §b7th tier§6 of each milestone.");
        provider.add("gtna.godforge.gui.inversioninfotext.3",
                "The Composition milestone is once again an exception, as that continues to scale by 1 each tier, with its own formula for calculating progress. Each module type is given a value, ranging from §b1§6 for the Helioflare Power Forge to §b5§6 for the Heliofusion Exoticizer in Magmatter Mode, then the amount of each module present is subtracted by 1 and multiplied by its value. These values are added up and divided by 5, this is the final milestone tier on top of the base 7.");
